===persian===

از مشبکِ چشمانت
باغِ پاییزی‌ام چه زیباست.
آسمانِ خاطرت اما، ابری‌ست.
تو به موهایِ سپیدِ من نگاه می‌کنی
و به آفتاب می‌اندیشی.
یک قطره از نگاهت
به چشمانم می‌افتد...
من چشمانم را می‌بندم...
گرم می‌شوم...
و با غرور به تو می‌اندیشم.
سبز و سرخ پنجاه بهار...
در آسمانِ خاکستری...
دی ماه ۱۳۶۹

===machine===

Through the lattice of your eyes
how beautiful my autumn garden is.
But the sky of your memory is clouded.
You look at my white hair
and think of the sun.
A drop from your gaze
falls into my eyes...
I close my eyes...
I grow warm...
and with pride I think of you.
Green and red, fifty springs...
in a gray sky...
Dey 1369

===lantern===

Seen through the lattice of your eyes
how beautiful my autumn garden is.
But the sky of your remembering is overcast.
You look at my white hair
and you think of the sun.
One drop out of your gaze
falls into my eyes...
I close my eyes...
I grow warm...
and think of you with pride.
Green and red, fifty springs...
in a gray sky...

Dey 1369

===translation===

===footnotes===

مشبک is the pierced lattice of a window screen, so her eyes are the grille he sees
his own autumn through. The close returns to the arithmetic of gray-gaze four pages earlier: green
and red, the two colours that cancel into gray, here fifty springs of them held in one gray sky.

